# Experimenting with ESP32 

## Audio-Visualizer/DAC

An attempt to create a simple, hight performance low memory footprint library of custom UI components. The project's UI mimics (more or less) RME ADI-2 UI.

The functionality (atm) includes I2S output, volume control, and a single input - an internet radio. The audio functionality in build entirely using <https://github.com/pschatzmann/arduino-audio-tools>. A truly outstanding project!

### Build

The build configurations support ESP32/ESP32-S3/ESP32-P4 and local development on MACOS (Win/Linux can be easily added, SDL2 is the only dependency). Supported displays are 'ST7735', 'ST7735V', 'ILI9341' (including IPS model without CS pin).

Not all displays work well with all graphic libraries. Hence a possibility to swap library via a singe define:

Render via LovyanGFX:
```
lib_deps = 
  ${env.lib_deps}
  https://github.com/lovyan03/LovyanGFX.git#develop
...

build_flags = 
  ${env.build_flags}
  -D LGFX_BACKEND=1
```
Render via Arduino_GFX:
```
lib_deps = 
  ${env.lib_deps}
	moononournation/GFX Library for Arduino@^1.6.7
...

build_flags = 
  ${env.build_flags}
  -DArduino_GFX_BACKEND
```
Render via TFT_eSPI:
```
lib_deps = 
  ${env.lib_deps}
  TFT_eSPI
...

build_flags = 
  ${env.build_flags}
  -DTFT_eSPI_BACKEND
```

Render via Adafruit's GFX:
```
lib_deps = 
  ${env.lib_deps}
  https://github.com/adafruit/Adafruit-ST7735-Library.git@^1.11.0
...

build_flags = 
  ${env.build_flags}
  -DAGFX_BACKEND
```

### Build
* None of displays seem to work with ESP32-P4 using LovyanGFX. Adafruit's and Arduino GFX do work, although super slow. Seems like a problem with HWSPI.